  "notes": "Low-register nu-disco pop, and the lane's own boundary case — the orientation keeps her here rather than in `dance-pop` because the records are topline-first even over a four-on-the-floor kick. The drums are authored from the entry word for word: \"four-on-the-floor kick with the low end used sparingly and a fill placed after every fourth measure\" is `anchors` on all four beats with `fills.smallEveryBars` 4; \"handclaps, cowbell and crowd noise as the percussion signature\" is the perc lane list; \"disco hat on offbeat 8ths opening to 16ths in the chorus\" is the weighted `hihat.base` plus a high `openHat.prob` on the offbeats. The low end is the identity claim and it is emphatically not an 808 — \"a MIDI-programmed funk bassline made to sound played … bass is the primary countermelody and moves in syncopated 16ths against a static kick\" — so `bassline.rhythm` is `independent_riff` at a low `followRootsProb` with a wide passing-tone set, and no `drums.bass808` block exists so the parent's explicit null stands. Harmony is \"4-bar minor vamps with 7ths and added 9ths\", which is the low `triad` share. Melody register is the documented working span: A3—D5 and F♯3—B4, \"a working span of roughly an 11th and almost never above D5\", so the ceiling is a hard 74. \"Melisma is used at phrase ends but she does not modulate\" is `endVariation`. The counter is the string-stab/vocoder answer the entry names. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize pair and the perc gain; the research gives a groove description, not numbers. ⚠ The BPM band is catalogue-derived and carries the research's [LOW-CONF] mark; `bpm.mode` 122 is the stated cluster centre (120—124) rather than an inference.",
